  "id": "DrugBank_DB01194 - MONDO_6875",
  "verbalization": "Brinzolamide appears to be associated with Ocular Hypertension through a mechanism involving side effects that are linked to the condition. The evidence suggests that Brinzolamide may contribute to Ocular Hypertension via the side effect of Loss Of Eyelashes, which is associated with both Bimatoprost and Travoprost, both of which are known to be used in the treatment of Ocular Hypertension. These compounds are typically used as prostaglandin analogs to lower intraocular pressure, and their use in this context implies a potential mechanism of action that could influence ocular pressure regulation. The presence of these side effects, coupled with the indication for Ocular Hypertension, supports a possible relationship between Brinzolamide and the condition, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of considering side effects in the context of drug repurposing, as they may provide indirect evidence of a therapeutic relationship.",
